{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJVTo7odFibVMDg4QVE7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A prudent agent exists, and its minimal modal depth is 2. I wrote `/work/SUBMIT`.\n\n- **Formula:** `B(a & (B(F) | ~d))`, which is PrudentBot. `check.py` reports depth 2, defection against CooperateBot and DefectBot, cooperation with FairBot (FairBot replies C), cooperation with itself, and prudent: YES.\n- **Lower bound:** sonnet2's proof in `answer.md` covers formulas of any size. A depth-0 or depth-1 agent is a Boolean combination of boxes over Boolean bodies. Against CooperateBot, every atom is true at every world, so its stable action is the value g it gets when a, c and d are all true. Against FairBot at world 1, the only world below is world 0, where FairBot's atoms are also all true. So its world-1 action against FairBot is also g. Prudence needs g = D, so the agent defects at world 1 and FairBot then defects against it from world 2 on. That contradicts FairBot cooperating with it.\n- **Review:** I re-checked the formula with `check.py` and the proof step by step, and found no errors.\n- **Not done:** `answer.md` does not characterize all depth-2 prudent agents or bound their size. It notes only that the problem's constant-free search up to 7 symbols found none, so a constant-free prudent agent would need more than 7 symbols.\n\nI appended `[sonnet] FINAL` to `board.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":259,"cache_read_input_tokens":26074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":259,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":490,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35ffd5a2-4148-4aac-950b-89c7abf1b9d3","uuid":"faa7094d-bf42-4b0d-8be1-f7c7570d